<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>

<div class="container-xl">
  <article class="legal">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: <%= lastUpdated %></p>
    <p>
      This Cookie Policy explains how Travel Roots uses cookies and similar technologies when you visit our website,
      what each one does, and how you can control them. It should be read together with our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#what">What cookies are</a></li>
        <li><a href="#necessary">Strictly necessary cookies</a></li>
        <li><a href="#preferences-storage">Preference storage</a></li>
        <li><a href="#third-party">Third-party services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#not-used">What we do not use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#preferences">Manage your preferences</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="what">1. What cookies are</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files that a website stores in your browser. Similar technologies, such as the
      browser's local storage, let a site remember information on your device. We use both only where they are
      needed to run the service or where you have given permission.
    </p>

    <h2 id="necessary">2. Strictly necessary cookies</h2>
    <p>
      These cookies are essential for the website to work and to keep it secure. They cannot be switched off
      because sign-in, form protection and checkout would stop working without them. They are set by Travel Roots
      only.
    </p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>tr.sid</code></td>
            <td>
              Identifies your session so you stay signed in. It also holds the security token that protects forms
              against cross-site request forgery and short-lived on-screen messages. It is marked HttpOnly and, in
              production, Secure, so scripts cannot read it and it is only sent over HTTPS. It is created only when it
              is needed, for example when you open a form or sign in.
            </td>
            <td>Expires 7 days after your last visit</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>tr_consent</code></td>
            <td>Records the choice you make in the cookie banner so we do not ask again on every page.</td>
            <td>180 days</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="preferences-storage">3. Preference storage</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose "Accept all", or enable preferences below, we save the following display settings in your
      browser's local storage. They never leave your device and are deleted as soon as you withdraw consent.
    </p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>tr-theme</code></td><td>Remembers whether you prefer the light or dark theme.</td><td>Until you clear it or withdraw consent</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tr-show-tax</code></td><td>Remembers whether prices are shown including GST.</td><td>Until you clear it or withdraw consent</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Without consent, these settings still work for the page you are on but are not remembered.</p>

    <h2 id="third-party">4. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Some features load content from trusted providers. These providers may receive your IP address and may set
      their own cookies on their own domains under their own policies:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> runs the secure payment window when you book a stay and may use cookies for fraud prevention and security.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> and <strong>GitHub</strong> are contacted only if you choose to sign in with them.</li>
      <li><strong>OpenStreetMap</strong> supplies the map tiles on listing pages.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>, <strong>Cloudinary</strong> and <strong>Unsplash</strong> deliver fonts and images.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="not-used">5. What we do not use</h2>
    <p>
      Travel Roots does not use advertising cookies, cross-site tracking, social media pixels or third-party
      analytics. If this changes, we will update this policy and ask for your consent first.
    </p>

    <h2 id="preferences">6. Manage your preferences</h2>
    <form id="cookiePreferencesForm" class="surface p-4 my-3">
      <div class="form-check form-switch mb-3">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="consentNecessary" checked disabled />
        <label class="form-check-label" for="consentNecessary">
          <strong>Strictly necessary</strong><br />
          <span class="text-muted small">Always on. Required for sign-in, security and payments.</span>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="form-check form-switch mb-4">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="consentPreferences" />
        <label class="form-check-label" for="consentPreferences">
          <strong>Preferences</strong><br />
          <span class="text-muted small">Remember your theme and tax display settings on this device.</span>
        </label>
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save preferences</button>
      <span class="ms-2 text-success small" data-saved-notice hidden>Your preferences have been saved.</span>
    </form>
    <p>
      You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies will
      prevent you from signing in and booking.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">7. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when we change how the website works. The date at the top shows when it was last
      revised. Questions are welcome at <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
